A developer is asked to add payment processing backed by the company's internal ledger system -- the only payment method the product supports today, with no second provider planned or announced. The developer submits this design:

```java
public interface PaymentGateway {
    ChargeResult charge(ChargeRequest request);
    RefundResult refund(RefundRequest request);
    String tokenize(PaymentMethod method);
    boolean supportsRecurring();
    boolean supportsPartialCapture();
}

public class InternalLedgerGateway implements PaymentGateway {
    // the only implementation that exists or is planned
}
```

The justification given is: "We might add Stripe or PayPal later, so building the interface now will save time." Which principle is most directly relevant to evaluating this decision, and what does it recommend here?
